WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
- [Zac] Originally from California,

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.100
Billy Hargrove was born
in 1967... in California.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.430
The city - in California
- that Billy grew up in

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.150
is never mentioned, but it's most likely

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.100
somewhere in Southern California,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.891
based on Billy's penchant for surfing.

00:00:12.891 --> 00:00:14.310
In California.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.563
DUSTIN: Yeah, totally tubular.
What, did I say that right?

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:20.400
Or is it like tubular?
(elongates the pronunciation)

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.740
- [Zac] The name of Billy's birth mother

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.770
remains unknown,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.190
but what is known is that Billy

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.540
would have been very close
to her as a small child.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.650
Billy's happiest memory

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.580
is from when he was about
seven or eight years old.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.500
He was surfing, while his
mother cheered him on.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.240
Billy brags about surfing a
wave that was seven feet tall.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.360
His Mom says she saw it

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.170
and he almost gave her a heart attack.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.450
Billy asks if he can keep
surfing for 10 more minutes,

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.527
and his Mom reluctantly agrees, saying,

00:00:41.527 --> 00:00:43.870
"Any longer than that
and Dad's gonna be mad."

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.990
It would be that very fury from
Billy's dad, Neil Hargrove,

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.140
that shaped him into who he would become.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.270
To learn more about Billy,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.910
and what makes him one of
Hawkins' scariest antagonists,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.401
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:55.401 --> 00:00:58.151
(metal music)

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.400
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.190
In this episode I'll be
covering the childhood,

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.197
life and end of Hawkins'

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.530
most intimidating high school student:

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.400
Billy Hargrove.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.370
I've mentioned in other
videos on Stranger Things,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.910
that Stephen King is a huge
influence for the show,

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.700
from the town of Hawkins
itself to specific characters.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.450
Billy is far from an exception.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.530
The Duffer Brothers, the
creators of "Stranger Things",

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.307
cited King directly when
coming up with Billy, stating:

00:01:22.307 --> 00:01:24.897
"Stephen King always has
really great human villains.

00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:26.927
"The evil in the real
world is often as bad

00:01:26.927 --> 00:01:28.617
"or worse than the supernatural evil,

00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:30.740
"so we wanted to include
a character like that."

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.150
So, it comes as no surprise

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.880
that Billy shares a lot of similarities

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.300
with some of King's
ugliest child antagonists.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.980
He even shares the same name
as Billy Nolan from Carrie.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.260
But Billy Hargrove possibly
has the most in common

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.670
with Henry Bowers from "IT".

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.200
From the more than tough fathers,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.070
to their views on those that
are different than them,

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.470
and treatment of those they
see as weaker than them,

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.320
there are a lot of parallels you can draw.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.050
To fully understand Billy
and what makes him so scary,

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.239
I'm gonna take it back to his upbringing.

00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:58.156
(mysterious music)

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.840
Billy's Dad, Neil, was a
little bit on the tough side,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:03.800
to say the least.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.380
Billy played baseball as a kid,
on a team called The Tigers.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.398
His Dad was extremely
critical of his performance,

00:02:08.398 --> 00:02:10.480
often yelling at him if he didn't perform

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.650
up to expectations.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.740
Because of this, Billy
grew up afraid of his Dad,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.300
as did his mother.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.200
NEIL: Where were you last
night? Where were you?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.833
MRS H: I told you! I was with Wendy.

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:21.395
NEIL: Stop lying to me!

00:02:21.395 --> 00:02:22.803
MRS H: I'm not lying to you!

00:02:22.803 --> 00:02:25.720
Get away from me! I said Get away!"

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.500
Neil Hargrove went on to re-marry,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.690
giving Billy a new step-mom
and a step-sister named Maxine.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.600
Billy is full of anger and resentment

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.620
towards this new family.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.900
It was never his fault that
his parents got divorced

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.180
and now he's being asked
to accept this new family

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.013
with open arms?

00:02:41.013 --> 00:02:43.330
Maxine often finds herself
on the receiving end

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.780
of Billy's teenage angst.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.810
In October of 1984, when
Billy was seventeen years old,

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.080
Neil moves the family to Hawkins, Indiana.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.100
Hawkins has the feeling
of a Stephen King town

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.080
in that it is frightening
for the kids that live there,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.260
because they not only have
to deal with the Upside Down,

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.650
Demogorgons and the Mind Flayer,

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.960
but there are also a
multitude of human monsters

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:00.840
to look out for.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.610
On October 28th, 1984
Billy's parents force him

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.670
to drive Max to school

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.460
and their resentment
for each other is clear,

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.940
based on how Max slams
the door and storms off

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.486
on the first day of their
respective new schools.

00:03:11.486 --> 00:03:16.094
(heavy metal music plays)

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.300
Billy drives a blue Camaro,
not unlike the blue muscle car

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.200
seen in the Muschietti adaptation of IT

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.820
driven around by the Bowers gang.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.320
He even has the look of several

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.880
of Stephen King's bully characters.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.950
The jeans, boots, even style of shirt,

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.960
is similar to Ace
Merrill from Stand By Me.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.500
This is a very specific choice

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.960
in that Billy both demonstrates
a popular look and trend

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.870
of the early 80s, but also could pass

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.383
as an Ace Merrill type from the 60s.

00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:40.770
This look is what draws
the attention of everyone.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:43.122
- Who is that?

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:48.122
- I have no idea but would
you check out that butt?

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:50.620
Just look at it go.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.670
- [Zac] The women of Hawkins
may be awestruck by Billy,

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.520
and he repeatedly puts himself on display

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:55.600
for this kind of attention.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.410
But in another parallel to Ace Merrill,

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.020
Billy has no respect for women

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.090
and he makes that abundantly clear.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.170
- You smell that Max. That's
actually (beep). Cow (beep).

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.003
- I don't see any cows.

00:04:06.003 --> 00:04:08.480
- Clearly, you haven't
met the high school girls.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.313
- [Zac] Yikes!

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:10.560
Another commonality he shares with Ace

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.770
can be seen in one of the
most tense scenes in the film,

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.033
which is not featured in the
novella that inspired it.

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:18.080
Ace plays chicken with an
oncoming log truck to win a race.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.730
He shows absolute determination,

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.349
and no fear or concern at
the possibility of killing

00:04:22.349 --> 00:04:25.163
everyone in the car, despite
their pleas for him to stop.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.380
Stranger Things has a moment
that looks almost identical.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.630
On Halloween, Billy
torments Max by threatening

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.910
to run Will, Lucas and
Dustin off of the road,

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.743
never letting up,

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:40.207
with the same unrelenting
determination as Ace.

00:04:42.787 --> 00:04:45.454
(wheels squeal)

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.090
- Yeah! That was a close one, huh?

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.950
- [Zac] But Max, Will, Dustin and Lucas

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.660
are not the only ones to end
up in Billy's crosshairs.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.400
Billy likes attention and
draws a lot of it himself.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.110
This is evident in the way he dresses,

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.590
the way he revs his engine
upon pulling into the school

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.710
and I could go on.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.490
So, when Billy hears that Steve Harrington

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.500
is the most popular guy
at Hawkins High School,

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.620
he immediately perceives Steve

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.860
as someone he needs to dominate.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.990
And what better place for a
legendary rivalry to begin,

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.196
than that year's Halloween party?

00:05:14.196 --> 00:05:16.463
(crowd cheering)

00:05:22.971 --> 00:05:25.888
(mysterious music)

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.130
Billy's quest to overtake
Steve's reputation

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.810
begins at the big Halloween party,

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.550
where Billy infiltrates
Steve's friend group

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.430
by beating Steve's record at keg stands,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.110
impressing Steve's friends.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.620
TOMMY: We got ourselves a
new Keg King, Harrington.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.510
- Yeah, that's right.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.360
- Yeah, eat it, Harrington.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.260
- [Zac] Apparently in Hawkins,

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:44.430
all you have to do to get a
group of friends to drop one

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.700
is be really good at
chugging beer upside down.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.270
But Billy's determination
to dominate Steve Harrington

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.370
doesn't stop there.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.370
The next day the two
have gym class together,

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.460
where Billy repeatedly
makes verbal jabs at him

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.230
and even aggressively knocks him down,

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.200
telling him to plant his
feet better next time.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.540
Man, they're playing like
it's the 90s out there!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.960
Oh yeah, it's still the 80s in this show.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.800
It comes as no surprise that
when, just a few days later,

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.970
Billy overhears that
Nancy, Steve's girlfriend,

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.770
was seen ditching school with another guy.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.920
Billy takes this as another
opportunity to emasculate Steve.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.151
BILLY: Don't take it too hard man.

00:06:15.151 --> 00:06:17.596
A pretty boy like you has
nothing to worry about.

00:06:17.596 --> 00:06:20.428
Plenty of (beep) in the sea.

00:06:20.428 --> 00:06:21.963
I'll be sure to leave you some.

00:06:21.963 --> 00:06:24.290
- [Zac] I can't help but be reminded again

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.877
of Ace from Stand by Me.

00:06:25.877 --> 00:06:29.090
EYEBALL: So, what's with you
and this Connie Palermo chick?

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.200
JACK: Eh, I've been seeing
her for a month now,

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.310
and all she'll let me do is feel her tits.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.060
ACE: She's a Catholic man.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.877
If you wanna get laid, you
gotta get yourself a Protestant.

00:06:39.877 --> 00:06:41.020
- [Zac] But it's also something

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.230
Billy probably picked up from his own Dad.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.520
Neil at one point tells
Billy to cancel a date

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.379
with whatever harlot he's seeing tonight.

00:06:47.379 --> 00:06:49.010
He used a different word.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.390
Sadly, misogyny is not
the only negative trait

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.200
that Billy takes on,
that he likely learned

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.210
from Neil Hargrove.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.250
Billy rarely pays attention to anything

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.660
his step-sister Max does,

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.590
but on November 2nd, 1984,
when Billy notices Max

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.780
having a heated discussion
with Lucas Sinclair,

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.170
he suddenly takes an
interest in Max's social life

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.750
and makes it clear that he disapproves

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.260
of her spending time with Lucas.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:11.030
In fact, of everyone that Billy
interacts with in Hawkins,

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.750
it seems like he harbors the
most disdain towards Lucas,

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.720
without really knowing anything about him.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.323
The scene kind of made me
wonder if it was a race thing.

00:07:20.223 --> 00:07:23.910
- Hey! This is serious (beep) okay?

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.023
I'm older than you,
and something you learn

00:07:26.023 --> 00:07:28.830
is that there are certain
types of people in this world

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.177
that you stay away from.

00:07:30.177 --> 00:07:31.453
And that kid, Max.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.850
That kid is one of them.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.300
- [Zac] The actor, Dacre Montgomery,

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.810
has stated that Billy's real
reason for not liking Lucas

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.577
has more to do with Lucas
seeming to have a crush on Max.

00:07:41.577 --> 00:07:42.687
"He loves his sister Max,

00:07:42.687 --> 00:07:44.227
"and if it were any
other kid bothering her

00:07:44.227 --> 00:07:45.850
"he would have reacted the same way."

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.390
It's kind of a strange answer,

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.710
because Billy hasn't been shown

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.600
to care about his
step-sister up to this point,

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.302
and he doesn't share the
same attitude for Dustin,

00:07:52.302 --> 00:07:54.260
who also shows interest in Max.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.710
But if Billy's feeling towards Lucas

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.000
are partially race related,

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.310
it would be another parallel to the way

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.330
that Henry Bowers treats and
thinks of Mike Hanlon in IT.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.500
In the case of Henry Bowers,

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.570
the racism is directly
learned from his Dad.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.050
And even if Billy isn't racist,

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:07.930
he definitely picked up
some prejudiced views

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:08.960
from his own father.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.130
Unfortunately for Max,

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.100
she has a second interaction
like this with Billy

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.130
the very next day. In
addition to being forced

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.500
to take Max to and from school,

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.460
it's also Billy's
responsibility to pick her up

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.293
from the arcade.

00:08:18.293 --> 00:08:20.240
Max tries to keep Billy
from being able to see

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.480
that she had been talking to Lucas,

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.810
but Billy still catches them.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.246
BILLY: What the hell did I tell you?

00:08:24.246 --> 00:08:26.746
MAX: It's a small town,
okay? We weren't hanging out.

00:08:27.775 --> 00:08:30.210
BILLY: You know what happens when you lie.

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:31.710
- [Zac] Even this warning about lying

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.850
comes from the influence of Neil Hargrove.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.910
When Billy was growing up,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.800
Neil Hargrove would accuse
Billy's mother of lying

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.540
and there were consequences
when he thought she was.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:40.520
Apparently in this case,

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.990
the consequence for Max
is a broken skateboard.

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.480
Billy's warning does not
fall on deaf ears with Max,

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.760
however, she doesn't
communicate this to Lucas.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.161
And who can really blame her?

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.060
What would that conversation look like?

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.980
It's easier for her to
just not mention it.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.010
As I mentioned, one of
Billy's defining traits

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.360
is his love for attention.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.970
He's very focused on his appearance,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.290
so he's often working out,
yet smoking as he does so,

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.000
which kind of defeats the purpose.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.150
I bet he would get along with Kat

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.700
from Final Destination 2.
But, despite taking smoke

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.550
directly into his lungs while working out,

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.500
his work is apparently so profuse,

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:13.150
that he refuses to be interrupted
when the doorbell rings.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.570
Max abruptly shuts the door,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.180
so Billy can tell something is up,

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:18.460
sending him to drop his
work out and investigate.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:20.510
But only after also cracking open a beer?

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:21.950
It feels like everything this guy does

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.410
is counterproductive to his workout.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.000
I mean, I would go on further about this,

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.580
but I've actually seen people drinking

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.380
sugar filled energy drinks at the gym.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.160
Maybe these people are just so powerful

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.980
that they have to set
themselves back a little bit

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.410
to give the rest of us a chance.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.243
Or maybe they're just fu-

00:09:34.243 --> 00:09:35.456
BILLY: Who the hell were you talking to?

00:09:35.456 --> 00:09:37.239
MAX: Mormons.

00:09:37.239 --> 00:09:38.373
- Mormons?

00:09:38.373 --> 00:09:39.770
- Talkative ones.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.230
- [Zac] After this, he leaves her to it,

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.550
but when Billy's Dad and Step-Mom

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:43.660
come home later that night,

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.360
they notice Max is missing
and Neil blames Billy

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.370
for not watching her.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.470
NEIL: So that's why you've
been staring at yourself

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.303
in the mirror like some (beep)

00:09:50.303 --> 00:09:51.750
instead of watching your sister?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.230
- You had one job Billy!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.060
I think Neil also has a lot in common

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.670
with Webby Garton, from IT.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:58.330
Webby was part of the gang responsible

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.440
for the death of a gay
man named Adrian Melon.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.780
I analyzed the whole situation

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.770
in Adrian's own episode of Horror History.

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.030
Neil seems to have the
same heterosexist outlook,

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:07.520
which may have rubbed off on his son.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.070
Just one of the many weird, just weird,

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:12.120
messed up issues that Billy seems to have.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.593
And another would soon make itself known.

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:22.302
(mysterious music)

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.240
Billy's Dad sends him to
find his missing step-sister,

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.500
and while going from door to door,

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.230
he makes a stop at the Wheeler
house to see if Max is there,

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.521
allowing him to have this

00:10:31.521 --> 00:10:36.063
statutory exchange with Mike
and Nancy's Mom, Karen Wheeler.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:40.490
- Oh, hi.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.323
- Hi.

00:10:41.323 --> 00:10:43.990
- I didn't realize that
Nancy had a sister.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.470
- I'm Nancy's mother.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.010
- No.
- Yes.

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:48.380
- Mrs. Wheeler.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.410
- I'm sorry, and you are?

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.610
- Billy. Billy Hargrove.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.100
- You must be here for Nancy.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.140
- Nancy? No, not my type.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:57.973
- [Zac] Well, honestly

00:10:57.973 --> 00:10:59.040
he kinda dodged a bullet there.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.410
After Billy gets the information
he needs from Mrs. Wheeler,

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.020
he moves on to the Byers' house.

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.905
As usual Billy wants all eyes
on him and he revs his engine.

00:11:05.905 --> 00:11:08.630
This has the desired effect
and Max starts to panic,

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:11.260
saying that Billy will kill
her and probably everyone else,

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.860
if he realizes she's there.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.890
It's up to Steve
Harrington to divert Billy

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:15.760
away from the house,

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.370
so he goes outside to confront him.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.740
Once again, Billy does his best

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.150
to assert dominance over his new rival.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:22.440
- This whole situation, Harrington.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:25.730
I don't know. It's giving
me the heebie jeebies.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:26.740
- Oh yeah? Why's that?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.737
- My 13 year old sister
goes missing all day,

00:11:28.737 --> 00:11:33.343
and then I find her with
you, in a stranger's house,

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:36.450
and you lie to me about it.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:37.470
- [Zac] Kind of a bold statement

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.430
for a teenager who just
told a much older woman

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.460
that a girl his own age is not his type.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.230
But Billy does manage to once again

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.440
assert dominance over Steve,

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.340
by hitting him so hard
he's knocked to the ground,

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:48.710
citing again that Steve
should have planted his feet.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:50.760
Considering that Billy
seems threatened by Steve,

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.230
you'd think Steve would be
the main target of his anger,

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.630
but Billy's real anger comes out at Lucas

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:57.577
and it is truly terrifying.

00:11:57.577 --> 00:12:02.323
BILLY: Well, well, well. Lucas
Sinclair, what a surprise.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.960
I thought I told you to
stay away from him, Max.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.058
- Billy, go away.

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:07.416
- You disobeyed me.

00:12:07.416 --> 00:12:10.098
And you what happens when you disobey me?

00:12:10.098 --> 00:12:10.931
- Billy-

00:12:10.931 --> 00:12:11.810
- I break things.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.080
- [Zac] But luckily for Lucas,

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.540
Steve Harrington isn't done.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.650
Just when it seems like Lucas
might be in real trouble,

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.370
Steve unexpectedly grabs Billy,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.531
managing to at least
redirect Billy's rage.

00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:22.680
As Steve lies helpless on the ground

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.020
after being pummeled by Billy,

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:26.840
Max notices a syringe left
over from the Hawkins lab

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.820
and injects the contents into his neck.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.480
And honestly, it's not completely clear

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.990
that Max even knew what
was in the syringe.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:34.280
Aside from the possibility

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.010
that it's something completely dangerous

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.120
and she could have been responsible

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:38.170
for whatever happened to him,

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.900
what if it was some kind of steroid

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.130
that would have just made
him stronger and more angry?

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.420
Or what if it caused him to slowly

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:45.680
turn into Grimace from the
McDonald's commercials?

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.460
It could have been really, really bad.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.580
But luckily, it's just a tranquilizer,

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.330
so Billy woke up a few hours later

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.290
in the locker room of the
Hawkins pool and heard

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.850
- [Jigsaw] I want to play a game.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:55.683
- No, I'm kidding.

00:12:55.683 --> 00:12:56.770
As the sedative takes effect,

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:58.720
instead of getting scared or even angry,

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.070
he starts laughing, which
is much more creepy.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:02.270
As he collapses to the floor,

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:04.030
she delivers more than a stern warning

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:06.243
for Billy to leave her
and her friends alone.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.700
He doesn't object as
his younger step-sister

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:10.940
proceeds to steal his car,

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.910
and pretty much leaves
Lucas alone after that

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.200
and lays low throughout the
next year at Hawkins High.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.590
But Billy, always vying
to be in the public eye,

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.280
doesn't stay out of it for long.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:20.840
In the Summer of 1985,

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.190
he gets a job as a
lifeguard at the local pool.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:27.303
- Lol.

00:13:27.303 --> 00:13:28.136
Karen Wheeler is no longer

00:13:28.136 --> 00:13:29.690
the only adult woman in Hawkins

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.320
to take an interest in Billy.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:34.163
- Ladies, she's coming down.

00:13:35.139 --> 00:13:38.222
- (sexy music plays)

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.050
- [Zac] However, Karen may be

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.360
the only woman whose
interest seems to be mutual.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.940
She purposely swims when
she knows he's watching

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.700
and he takes the bait,
inviting her to meet him

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.750
at a hotel at nights for swimming lessons.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.090
Which makes me wonder, I mean
they're already at a pool.

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:56.970
Why don't they just do
swimming lessons right he-

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:59.425
Oh, he's talking about se-

00:13:59.425 --> 00:14:00.750
As Billy drives to the hotel,

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.400
his car hits something in the road.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.490
Unfortunately, it wasn't Nancy,
or Lucas's little sister.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.540
In fact, it doesn't seem to be anything.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:08.790
As he gets out, he is pulled

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.140
by another powerful creature
from the Upside-Down,

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.948
the Mind Flayer, into the
Brimborn Steelworks Warehouse,

00:14:13.948 --> 00:14:15.773
where it's able to occupy Billy,

00:14:15.773 --> 00:14:17.850
similar to what it did to
Will Byers the previous year.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:18.683
Unlike Will though,

00:14:18.683 --> 00:14:21.000
Billy has a direct conversation
with the Mind Flayer,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.190
which communicates with Billy

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.526
by giving him visions
of talking to himself.

00:14:24.526 --> 00:14:26.529
BILLY: I said, what do you want?

00:14:26.529 --> 00:14:30.660
FLAYED BILLY: To build.
I want you to build.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:31.968
- To build what?

00:14:31.968 --> 00:14:34.168
- What you see.

00:14:34.168 --> 00:14:35.920
- I don't understand.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.680
- In an interview with the New York Times,

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.550
Dacre Montgomery gave a little
bit of additional context:

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.300
For Flayed Billy, I did a lot of research

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.480
on bipolar disorder and
split personalities,

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:47.280
and how one personality controls
the other personalities.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.113
- [Zac] Yes, I'm aware

00:14:48.113 --> 00:14:50.170
that bipolar and dissociative
identity disorder

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.100
are not the same thing,

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.610
but feel free to leave 100 comments

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:53.760
telling me about it anyways.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.520
This direct conversation with himself

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.280
could be seen as a symbol for a struggle

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.640
with multiple mental health
issues, but this video,

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:00.990
I'll just focus on the one that seems

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:03.290
to be most persistent in
Stranger Things season 3:

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:04.350
bipolar disorder.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.260
He experiences all of the common traits

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.140
of someone being inhabited
by the Mind Flayer,

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:11.260
which makes Billy act in stark
contrast to his usual self.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.430
He is sensitive to light,

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.690
his skin literally burns
at being in the sun.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.620
This causes Billy to become an introvert

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.710
and someone who wants to avoid being seen.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:20.800
Definitely not the
Billy we've come to know

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:21.720
up to this point.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.070
According to the Mayo Clinic,

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.998
different variations of
bipolar disorder involve

00:15:24.998 --> 00:15:26.900
what are called manic episodes.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.240
At times, the person may
be abnormally upbeat,

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:31.370
jumpy or wired, having increased activity,

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.940
an exaggerated sense of well-being

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.430
and heightened self-confidence.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.660
But on the other side, there
are major depressive episodes

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.870
that include marked loss of interest,

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.550
feeling no pleasure in activities,

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.390
restlessness or slowed behavior,
feelings of worthlessness,

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:45.780
and decreased ability
to think or concentrate.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:48.360
Many of these traits show
themselves in "flayed Billy."

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.850
When he returns to work, he's
sluggish and doesn't seem

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:52.220
to like anyone noticing him.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.130
He even hides away in a back
room to avoid the public.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.510
This is even more evident
when Karen follows Billy

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.510
into the backroom and
attempts to apologize

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:00.380
for standing him up.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.360
Billy can't even bring
himself to look at her

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.970
and feels compelled to hurt her,

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.801
as he has a vision where he
slams her head into a wall.

00:16:06.801 --> 00:16:08.319
KAREN: I shouldn't have said that--

00:16:08.319 --> 00:16:10.090
SLAAAAAMMIN'!!!!

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.810
He exerts enough self
control to not do that

00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:14.484
and instead, leaves
Karen with a firm warning

00:16:14.484 --> 00:16:16.010
to stay away from him.

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.900
To this point, it seems
like Billy is going through

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:19.960
much of what Will went
through when he was occupied

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:22.890
by the Mind Flayer a year prior,
but this would soon change,

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:25.340
as the Mind Flayer realizes
a unique opportunity

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:26.923
that its new subject presents.

00:16:36.557 --> 00:16:37.390
Under the influence of

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.400
the massive entity of the Upside-Down,

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:42.210
Billy Hargrove is compelled to
bring other Hawkins residents

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:45.030
to the warehouse for the Mind
Flayer to occupy them, too.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.940
One victim of this would
be a fellow lifeguard

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.140
named Heather Holloway.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:49.390
FARNSWORTH: Go to hell Heather!

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.000
- [Zac] The next day
at the lifeguard chair,

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.620
Billy literally starts to burn up,

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:54.890
so he runs to the showers
to stand in the cold water,

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:57.127
and Heather runs after
him to see if he is okay,

00:16:57.127 --> 00:16:59.390
but the Mind Flayer
lives up to it's namesake

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.638
and distorts his perception of the events.

00:17:01.638 --> 00:17:03.220
- Take me to him!

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:05.520
- [Zac] Which he does.
After knocking her out cold,

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.980
he lays her down at the steel works

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.420
and tells her not to be afraid

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.656
and that it'll soon all be over.

00:17:10.656 --> 00:17:13.922
- Don't be afraid. It'll be over soon.

00:17:13.922 --> 00:17:15.264
(thumps)

00:17:15.264 --> 00:17:16.870
(screams)

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.310
- I think she might be afraid.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.030
After she joins the Mind Flayers ranks,

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:25.310
the two of them continue to
act like normal residents

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.840
as not to raise suspicion,
by filling the bathtub

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.210
with bags and bags of ice

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:30.890
to keep their body temperatures cool.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:32.730
The next targets are Heather's parents.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.040
When Eleven and Max, who realize
something is up with Billy,

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.270
arrive at the Holloway's house,

00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:38.330
Billy is no longer
acting sluggish and shy.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:40.410
He's upbeat, outgoing, and talkative.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.960
The Mind Flayer is active and
Billy is exhibiting traits

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.651
of a common manic episode. As
soon as Eleven and Max leave,

00:17:45.651 --> 00:17:49.100
only partially convinced by
Billy's seemingly innocent act,

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:51.630
Billy and Heather team up to
knock out Mr. and Mrs Holloway

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.500
and take them to the Brimborn Steel Works

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.984
and give the same warning.

00:17:54.984 --> 00:17:56.850
HEATHER: It'll all be over soon.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:58.910
- [Zac] At one point, Will
shares his experiences

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.050
of being possessed by the
Mind Flayer with his friends,

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.440
stating that those who are possessed

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.260
are kind of themselves
until the Mind Flayer

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:07.070
becomes active, a pattern that
seems to support my theory

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.180
that the creature's grip
on Billy is an allegory

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:11.950
for a manic or depressive
episode of bipolar disorder.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.100
I also find it interesting
that the kids make a plan

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.640
to draw the Mind Flayer out of Billy

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:18.430
by locking him in a sauna, as
the Mind Flayer hates heat.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:21.560
Literally bipolar. Their
plan almost even works,

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:24.350
as Billy is burning up in the
sauna he, for the first time,

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.670
shares vulnerability
with his step sister Max,

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.870
screaming repeatedly, "It's not my fault"

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.170
and "He made me do it."

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:32.540
Again, according to the
Mayo Clinic and other sites,

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.760
it's a common trait for
someone experiencing mania

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.440
to engage in reckless and
even compulsive behavior

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:38.340
they later regret.

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.980
When Max asks "Who made you do it?,"

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:42.560
Billy describes the Mind
Flayer as a giant shadow.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.100
Something that he can't articulate

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.690
and that is beyond his control.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.250
As Billy and Max share this moment

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.490
and Max explains to Billy that
they are trying to help him,

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:52.200
The Mind Flayer interrupts by
becoming "active" once again,

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:54.080
and Billy smashes the
glass door of the sauna

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.520
and lashes out at the kids.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.120
Eleven, with her psychokinetic powers,

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.810
is just barely able to save them,

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:01.080
but the battle seems to
use up most of her power.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.929
Billy meets up with
Heather shortly after this.

00:19:02.929 --> 00:19:04.648
- [Heather] The girl, was it her?

00:19:04.648 --> 00:19:07.350
- [Billy] Yeah. It was her. She knows now.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:11.080
She knows about me. She
could have killed me.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.700
- [Zac] Wait a minute. Aren't they both

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:14.480
under the control of the
Mind Flayer right here?

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.670
Like the Mind Flayer is just having

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.140
this conversation with itself?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.751
I guess maybe how this works
is everything they know

00:19:18.751 --> 00:19:21.720
is sent to the Mind
Flayer, but the Mind Flayer

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.260
doesn't necessarily send
information back to them.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.448
It may be for a good reason,
seeing as how Eleven is capable

00:19:26.448 --> 00:19:29.550
of going into their heads,
which she does, shortly after.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.500
She sees Billy's most intimate memories.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:33.390
How happy he was with
his mother on the beach

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.070
and how disturbing his father was.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.871
This goes on until the Mind
Flayer becomes active again,

00:19:36.871 --> 00:19:39.680
trapping Eleven in Billy's
head and taunting her

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.630
that it's coming for her.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.602
- And now it's time. Time to end it.

00:19:43.602 --> 00:19:46.157
And we are going to end you.

00:19:46.157 --> 00:19:48.150
- Eleven is able to fight back and escape,

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:50.010
but The Mind Flayer
now has enough strength

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.750
to leave Brimborn Steelworks Warehouse

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.900
and go after her itself. So it sends Billy

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.400
to track her and try to find her,

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:58.224
but he finds himself just one
step behind wherever she goes.

00:19:58.224 --> 00:20:00.920
Billy finally gets to
her after The Mind Flayer

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.910
finds Eleven on it's own and he shows up.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:05.180
The kids are trying to
escape from Starcourt Mall.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.810
In an attempt to intimidate
them he revs his engine.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:10.380
This may seem like the
old Billy, but it isn't.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:13.000
Billy is now completely
overtaken by the Mind Flayer

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.780
and floors it at Nancy, who
fires a gun directly at him,

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.090
but apparently misses him.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:20.023
But Billy's old nemesis, Steve
Harrington saves the day.

00:20:24.539 --> 00:20:27.340
Billy is badly hurt but still manages

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:29.740
to catch Mike and Max trying
to escape with Eleven.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.750
He's completely lost
control at this point,

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.120
throwing his own step sister
and Mike against a wall

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.610
and hitting Eleven's head
so hard he knocks her out.

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:38.150
He takes Eleven up to the food court

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:39.560
to present her to The Mind Flayer,

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:41.550
just as he had with Heather, her family

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.890
and likely several others,

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.980
but Eleven is able to connect
with him on a human level

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:47.580
by bringing up the memories
that he shared with her.

00:20:49.133 --> 00:20:51.053
- Seven feet.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:58.173
You told her the wave was seven feet.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:01.783
And you... you were happy.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.150
- In California!

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:06.340
It seems that Eleven has managed

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:07.980
to break through the
barrier in Billy's mind

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:09.400
and speak to the real Billy.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.450
After this moment of human connection,

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.470
Billy leaves El alone and stands up

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:14.950
to confront the Mind Flayer.

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:16.140
Using his bare hands,

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:17.820
he's actually able to
hold the monster off,

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:19.220
to protect Max and her friends.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.730
But he's only able to
withstand it for so long.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.560
The other appendages of this
terrifying creature jut out

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.700
and latch onto him,
rendering him immobile,

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.350
before finally one of its
arms shoots through his chest

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.370
and finishes him. Given the highs and lows

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:32.900
Billy was put through by this creature,

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.580
his fate could be allegory

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.700
for a losing battle with mental illness.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.986
His last words are to his sister Max,

00:21:38.986 --> 00:21:40.952
- I'm sorry.

00:21:40.952 --> 00:21:43.060
- [Zac] This moment of overcoming

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:45.410
an evil supernatural entity
that's possessing him

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:48.640
and letting love for family
override everything, briefly,

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:51.040
leading to a self sacrifice
sounds very similar

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.750
to Jack Torrance in The Shining:

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:55.490
The face in front of him
changed. It was hard to say how;

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.720
there was no melting or
merging of the features.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:21:59.518
The body trembled slightly,
and then the bloody hands

00:21:59.518 --> 00:22:01.840
opened like broken claws.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.150
The mallet fell from them
and thumped on the rug.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:06.630
That was all. But suddenly
his Daddy was there,

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.290
looking at him in mortal agony,

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.300
and sorry so great that Danny's heart

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.680
flamed within his chest.

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.557
The mouth drew down in a quivery bow.

00:22:13.557 --> 00:22:16.100
"Doc," Jack Torrance
said. "Run away quick.

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.630
And remember how much I love you."

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:19.370
That's not just a coincidence.

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:21.800
The Duffer brothers instructed
actor Dacre Montgomery

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.253
to specifically draw from Jack Torrance.

00:22:25.087 --> 00:22:26.140
- I was given a lot of
Jack Nicholson, yeah,

00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:28.570
a lot of like The Shining.
Because my character, I think,

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:31.470
in many ways, is kind of that
unpredictable sort of nature

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:33.210
that I think Jack Nicholson, sort of has.

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:35.300
- I find it fitting that
Billy, who seems to be

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:37.120
a melting pot of many of Stephen King's

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.310
greatest human villains,

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:40.260
ends his story in such a similar way

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:42.210
to perhaps the most iconic human villain

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.550
that King has ever created.

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:46.000
Despite being an awful
person for most of the story,

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.420
I think a lot of viewers find
his death to be a tragic one,

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:49.705
given how young he was, and of course,

00:22:49.705 --> 00:22:51.530
his late stage redemption arc.

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:53.140
And this isn't canon, but the next day,

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:55.180
Mrs. Wheeler cried for 14 hours,

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:57.210
lamenting in having missed her chance.

00:22:57.210 --> 00:22:58.620
If you want to see the histories

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.590
of more Stranger Things characters,

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:02.290
click that playlist on the left.

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:03.874
I've got at least one
more episode on the way,

00:23:03.874 --> 00:23:06.230
so remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.530
for new horrors every week,

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:09.740
ring the death bell for all notifications

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:14.740
and I'll see you in the next
one. Assuming we both survive.

00:23:14.894 --> 00:23:17.977
(techno music plays)

